1
00:00:02,770 --> 00:00:08,051
Teams and the team board. One goal system across many teams

2
00:00:08,603 --> 00:00:15,428
When several teams run the same goals, start by creating the teams, with sub-teams if you need them.

3
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:20,806
Open a team to add leads, who set targets, and members, who check in.

4
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:27,026
Then open the Team board, and pick the organization, the goal template and the cycle.

5
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:34,660
Rows are teams, columns are metrics. Each cell shows current against target, and the pace needed.

6
00:00:34,792 --> 00:00:40,723
Totals for each department and the whole organization are calculated from the teams.

7
00:00:40,857 --> 00:00:46,614
In Targets mode, set each team's start and target, then Save targets.

8
00:00:46,735 --> 00:00:51,342
In Check in mode, type every team's number, then Save check-ins.

9
00:00:51,448 --> 00:00:55,928
Show by week compares each period instead of running totals.

10
00:00:56,032 --> 00:00:59,571
Full screen shows just the board, for the team meeting.

11
00:01:01,177 --> 00:01:06,423
To define the goals once for every team, create a goal template with New.

12
00:01:10,583 --> 00:01:19,323
For each metric, choose how teams add up: add up, average, or lowest team. Then pick the teams, and create.
